{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For / his father's house.</b> His family." "<b>Let this be your covering.</b> Even though it is with a heh, it is like its fellows, and the meaning is: we do not ask you to give us a garment." "<b>And the stumbling-block.</b> The meaning concerns Jerusalem, and so it is written כי כשלה (Jeremiah 8:4), in the manner that a person speaks thus in a time of anger."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The heh in question is unclear from context; likely refers to a morphological feature of שמלה or its prefix."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:41.220677287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}